            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": ""
            },
            "description": "# TC012 – Login with Empty Password\n\n**Type:** UI Validation (Not Applicable for API)\n\n## Objective\n\nVerify that the application prevents login when the password field is left empty.\n\n## Why this is not automated in Postman\n\nThis validation is implemented in the React frontend before the API request is submitted. No request is sent to the backend.\n\n## Manual Steps\n\n1. Open the Login page.\n    \n2. Enter a valid registered email.\n    \n3. Leave the password field empty.\n    \n4. Click **Login**.\n    \n\n## Expected Result\n\n- Login request is blocked.\n    \n- A validation message is displayed for the password field.\n    \n- No API call is triggered.\n    \n\n**Manual Test Case:** TC012TC013 – Login with Empty Email\n\n**Type:** UI Validation (Not Applicable for API)\n\n## Objective\n\nVerify that the application prevents login when the email field is left empty.\n\n## Why this is not automated in Postman\n\nThis validation is handled by the React frontend and the browser before any API request is made.\n\n## Manual Steps\n\n1. Open the Login page.\n    \n2. Leave the email field empty.\n    \n3. Enter a valid password.\n    \n4. Click **Login**.\n    \n\n## Expected Result\n\n- Login request is blocked.\n    \n- A validation message is displayed for the email field.\n    \n- No API call is triggered.\n    \n\n**Manual Test Case:** TC013"
          },
          "response": []
