        {
          "name": "TC015_Browser_Back_AfterLogOut",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "description": "# TC015 – Browser Back After Logout\n\n**Type:** Manual Validation (UI + Session Security)\n\n## Objective\n\nVerify that a user cannot access the Dashboard by pressing the browser Back button after logging out.\n\n## Why this is not automated in Postman\n\nThis scenario depends on browser navigation history, protected routes, and session state. It is covered as a manual/UI test rather than a standalone API test.\n\n## Manual Steps\n\n1. Log in with a verified user.\n    \n2. Navigate to the Dashboard.\n    \n3. Click **Logout**.\n    \n4. Press the browser **Back** button.\n    \n\n## Expected Result\n\n- User is redirected to the Login/Home page.\n    \n- Dashboard is not displayed.\n    \n- The previous authenticated session cannot be restored using browser history.\n    \n\n**Manual Test Case:** TC015"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "TC017-Refresh-Dashboard",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": ""
            },
            "description": "# TC017 – Page Reload Session Persistence\n\n**Type:** Manual Validation (UI + API)\n\n## Objective\n\nVerify that reloading the application does not log out an authenticated user and the session is restored using the refresh token.\n\n## Why this is not automated in Postman\n\nThis scenario depends on browser behavior (page refresh, cookies, and React state restoration). It is covered as a manual/UI test rather than a standalone Postman API test.\n\n## Manual Steps\n\n1. Log in with a verified user.\n    \n2. Navigate to the Dashboard.\n    \n3. Refresh the browser page (F5 / Ctrl+R).\n    \n4. Verify the user remains logged in and the dashboard loads successfully.\n    \n\n## Expected Result\n\n- User session persists after reload.\n    \n- Dashboard is displayed without redirecting to Login.\n    \n- A new access token is obtained through the refresh token mechanism in the background.\n    \n\n**Manual Test Case:** TC017"
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
